.el .ds Aq '
.TH trellis-list 1 "" trellis "Trellis Manual"
.SH NAME
trellis\-list \- List packages in topological order (dependencies first)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrellis list\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-with\-dependents\fR] [\fB\-\-releasable\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List packages in topological order (dependencies first)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-directory\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Run as if started in this directory
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit JSON instead of name/lifecycle columns
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
When to color output. `auto` follows the terminal, `NO_COLOR`, and `CLICOLOR=0`; the other two override that detection
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<REF>\fR
Only packages owning files changed since this git ref
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress normal\-path output; JSON/report payloads and errors still print
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-dependents\fR
Add the reverse\-dependency closure of the selection
.TP
\fB\-\-releasable\fR
Only packages whose release lifecycle is `git_only` or `hex`
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Trace every command trellis shells out to, on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR
Don\*(Aqt check whether a newer trellis release is available

The check is also skipped in CI, when not attached to a terminal, and when `TRELLIS_NO_UPDATE_CHECK` or `DO_NOT_TRACK` is set.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
